==Culture==
The cultivar '[[Kimjongilia]]' is a floral emblem of [[North Korea]].

The species ''[[Begonia darthvaderiana]]'' was named for the [[Star Wars]] character.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2015-12-02 |title=The Darth Vader Begonia |url=https://www.indefenseofplants.com/blog/2015/12/2/the-darth-vader-begonia |access-date=2026-01-28 |website=In Defense of Plants |language=en-US}}</ref>

Most begonias are sour to the taste, and some people in some areas eat them. This is safe in small amounts but potentially toxic in large quantities due to the prevalence of [[oxalic acid]] in the tissues.{{sfnp|Laferrière|1990}}

In [[floriography]] begonias represent a warning, "we are being watched," "this must end,"<ref name="Darcey">{{cite book |last1=Darcey |first1=Cheralyn |title=Flowerpaedia |date=2018-03-01 |publisher=Rockpool |isbn=978-1-925429-46-6 |pages=159 |ref=Darcey}}</ref> "be careful," and/or "take heed."<ref name="Meaning">{{cite web |title=Meaning Of Begonia Flowers: Beauty, Emotions & Symbolism Unfolded |url=https://windflowerflorist.com/blogs/news/begonia-flowers-meaning?srsltid=AfmBOorxn-wt9VNlOw4K4FtVEs_RQKNPeSFLKzYL4D388HFW5lhjZ9Hy |website=Windflower |publisher=Windflower Florist |access-date=28 December 2025 |ref=Meaning}}</ref>

Bian Gong<!--Q15938085--> wrote a poem titled ''Begonia'', and [[Chen Chun]] wrote an ''Inscription on Begonia''. Begonias are associated with the love stories of [[Lu You]] and Wan Tang as well as a legend titled 采兰杂志(采兰, so begonias are symbolic of love in China.<ref name="Lingfei" /> 采兰杂志(采兰 (which translates roughly to 'gathering orchids' or 'gathering valuable information') lies within the [[Biji (Chinese literature)|Biji]] literary genre. It tells the story of a woman mourning the loss of her husband whose tears turn to begonias. The author is unknown and it's generally believed to come from before the [[Ming dynasty]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=琅嬛记卷中-琅嬛记全文原文-识典古籍 |url=https://www.shidianguji.com/ens/book/NA09677/chapter/1kcj7hlhijmrt?page_from=M_search_page&paragraphId=7440754887052279858&search_mode=content&keywords=%25E6%2581%2592,%25E6%2598%2594%25E6%259C%2589%25E5%25A9%25A6%25E4%25BA%25BA,%25E6%2598%2594%25E6%259C%2589%25E5%25A9%25A6%25E4%25BA%25BA%25EF%25BC%258C%25E6%2580%259D%25E6%2589%2580%25E6%25AD%25A1%25EF%25BC%258C%25E4%25B8%258D%25E8%25A6%258B%25EF%25BC%258C%25E8%25BC%2592%25E6%25B6%2595%25E6%25B3%25A3%25EF%25BC%258C%25E6%2581%2592%25E7%2581%2591%25E6%25B7%259A%25E4%25BA%258E%25E5%258C%2597%25E7%2589%2586%25E4%25B9%258B%25E4%25B8%258B,%25E5%25A9%25A6%25E4%25BA%25BA,%25E6%2580%259D%25E6%2589%2580%25E6%25AD%25A1,%25E6%2589%2580%25E6%25AD%25A1,%25E4%25B8%258D%25E8%25A6%258B,%25E8%25BC%2592,%25E8%25BC%2592%25E6%25B6%2595%25E6%25B3%25A3,%25E6%25B6%2595%25E6%25B3%25A3,%25E6%2581%2592%25E7%2581%2591%25E6%25B7%259A%25E4%25BA%258E%25E5%258C%2597%25E7%2589%2586%25E4%25B9%258B%25E4%25B8%258B,%25E7%2581%2591%25E6%25B7%259A,%25E7%2589%2586&version=9&contentMatch=1 |access-date=2026-01-22 |website=www.shidianguji.com}}</ref>

{{Blockquote|text=昔有妇人怀人不见 (a long time ago there was a woman who missed her beloved but could not meet him)，恒洒泪于北墙之下。(she often cried and her tears fell beneath the northern wall) 后洒处生草 (Later plants grew where her tears had fallen)，其花甚媚 (the flowers were beautiful)，色如妇面(and their color was similar to her rosy cheek)，其叶正绿反红(the leaves were green on top and red underneath)，秋开(they bloomed in autumn)，名曰‘断肠花’(they were called heartbreaking flower)，即今‘秋海棠’也。(aka today's Begonia, 秋海棠)|author=Unknown|title=采兰杂志(采兰|source=}}

